1
00:01:20,352 --> 00:01:25,479
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْراً

2
00:01:25,611 --> 00:01:26,841
 اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ الله

3
00:01:31,881 --> 00:01:43,035
We will start with, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) and how he would deal with innovations in religion, Al-Biddah(ألبدعة)

4
00:01:45,892 --> 00:01:53,314
and this is still relating to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) and the society.

5
00:01:55,008 --> 00:02:01,055
Basically we'll spend a lot of time talking about the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب)

6
00:02:01,102 --> 00:02:03,955
how he approaches the society and how he dealt with them.

7
00:02:06,013 --> 00:02:09,651
And then after that we will talk about the Ghazawat(غزوات) that occurred

8
00:02:10,343 --> 00:02:14,829
in the time of Umar(عُمَر) and that would be the end of these sessions.

9
00:02:15,087 --> 00:02:18,613
Towards the end of the sessions, we will talk about the Ghazawat(غزوات).

10
00:02:23,993 --> 00:02:30,120
The people of Egypt went to Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص), their Governor.

11
00:02:32,230 --> 00:02:34,986
He was appointed governor over them by Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب).

12
00:02:37,677 --> 00:02:40,676
So, they went to Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) and they said;

13
00:02:42,105 --> 00:02:53,065
This river, the Nile does not flow unless we sacrifice for it.

14
00:02:55,945 --> 00:03:03,548
He said: Every year we have a young lady,

15
00:03:05,302 --> 00:03:12,178
we would go to her father and take her from him

16
00:03:12,725 --> 00:03:19,215
we give him back some money and we would put the best clothes on her and the best jewelry

17
00:03:20,042 --> 00:03:21,495
and then we would throw her into the river.

18
00:03:23,650 --> 00:03:29,974
These are traditions of Shirk(شرك) that existed in Egypt

19
00:03:30,649 --> 00:03:33,478
and they believed that it makes the river flow.

20
00:03:34,958 --> 00:03:41,519
So, they sacrifice this poor woman for the river and it makes it flow.

21
00:03:44,837 --> 00:03:48,893
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said: "Islam erases everything before it,

22
00:03:50,227 --> 00:03:56,434
and you are not allowed to practice such traditions as Muslims."

23
00:03:57,672 --> 00:04:01,220
So, he issued a ban on such a practice.

24
00:04:02,738 --> 00:04:08,642
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) it was a Qadar(قدر) of Allah, a test, that the water level went down.

25
00:04:11,779 --> 00:04:17,973
So, everybody started to saying, see because we didn’t sacrifice this woman,

26
00:04:18,643 --> 00:04:21,092
the river is not flowing.

27
00:04:24,023 --> 00:04:28,542
And Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) insisted on this prevention and ban

28
00:04:29,737 --> 00:04:33,475
and it got so bad the water level went so low

29
00:04:35,116 --> 00:04:40,551
that, the people were about to move, they were about to evacuate.

30
00:04:41,478 --> 00:04:46,087
Because you know the people in Egypt their lifeline is the Nile River.

31
00:04:46,701 --> 00:04:51,322
Egypt doesn’t really receive sufficient rain for agriculture.

32
00:04:52,069 --> 00:04:56,736
So, it is the lifeline for the people, that's how they live,

33
00:04:57,447 --> 00:04:59,368
it's water from the Nile river.

34
00:05:02,505 --> 00:05:06,288
So, Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) sends a letter to Ameer ul Mo'mineen(أمير المؤمنين), he said;

35
00:05:07,215 --> 00:05:10,194
This is the tradition that they had, and I banned it,

36
00:05:10,641 --> 00:05:12,661
and I told them that it is in Islam, it is Haram(خرام),

37
00:05:13,432 --> 00:05:15,646
so Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) sends him a letter back.

38
00:05:15,887 --> 00:05:18,375
He said: What you have done is the right thing

39
00:05:19,648 --> 00:05:25,790
and I am sending along with this letter a card, or piece of paper

40
00:05:27,807 --> 00:05:30,201
and I want you to throw it in the river.

41
00:05:33,461 --> 00:05:36,033
In that card Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) wrote:

42
00:05:38,305 --> 00:05:43,472
مِنْ عَبْدِالله امير المومنين عمر بن الخطاب اِلى نِيْلِ اَهْلِ الْمِصْر

43
00:05:44,588 --> 00:05:48,637
From the servant of Allah, the Ameer of Al-Mo'mineen(أمير المؤمنين),

44
00:05:48,906 --> 00:05:52,242
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) to the Nile of the people of Egypt.

45
00:05:53,280 --> 00:05:55,520
He is writing the river a letter.

46
00:05:59,296 --> 00:06:06,639
اِنْ كُنْتَ تَجْرِيْ بِأَمْرِكَ وَمِنْ قِبَلِكَ فَلَا تَجْرِيْ فَلَا حَاجَتَ لَنَا فِيْكْ

47
00:06:08,281 --> 00:06:14,572
If you are running of your own accord, then stop running because we don’t need you anymore.

48
00:06:16,094 --> 00:06:18,495
وَ إِنْ كُنْتَ تَجْرِيْ بِأَمْرِالله

49
00:06:18,981 --> 00:06:23,973
وَاللهُ هُوَّالَّذِيْ يُجْرِيْكَ، فَنَسْئَلُ اللهَ عَزُّوْجَلْ اَنْ يٌجْرِيْكَ

50
00:06:25,413 --> 00:06:31,774
And if you are running because Allahعَزّوجَلّ is the one making you run and flow

51
00:06:32,355 --> 00:06:35,602
then we ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to make you flow.

52
00:06:38,683 --> 00:06:43,192
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) takes this card and he throws it into the Nile River,

53
00:06:43,349 --> 00:06:51,533
within one day the Nile River went up sixteen diraa(درعا), within one day.

54
00:06:52,329 --> 00:06:57,081
Receiving a letter from Ameer ul Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين) it went up sixteen diraa(درعا).

55
00:06:57,217 --> 00:07:01,225
Diraa(درعا) is about foot long, actually more than a foot long.

56
00:07:05,275 --> 00:07:10,710
So, apparently, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) wasn't only the Ameer of Momineen(أمير المؤمنين),

57
00:07:11,631 --> 00:07:13,831
he was also the Ameer(أمير) of the Rivers.

58
00:07:16,559 --> 00:07:21,105
And this story was mentioned by Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) in Al-Bidaya Wan Nihayah(البداية ونهاية).

59
00:07:23,619 --> 00:07:30,563
So Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) stopped this evil tradition of sacrifice for the religion,

60
00:07:31,511 --> 00:07:35,073
this Shirk(شرك) in Allahعَزّوجَلّ, he made it Haram(حرام).

61
00:07:38,217 --> 00:07:42,668
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) when he kissed the black stone he said;

62
00:07:43,298 --> 00:07:47,600
اِنِّيْ لَا أَعْلَمُوْ أَنَّكَ حَجَرْ لَا تَنْفَعْ وَلَا تَضُرْ

63
00:07:48,079 --> 00:07:55,355
وَلَوْلَا أَنِّيْ رَاَيْتُ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يُقَبِّلُكْ مَا قَبَّلْتُكَ

64
00:07:57,558 --> 00:08:02,579
I know that you are rock, that cannot harm or benefit

65
00:08:03,607 --> 00:08:08,986
and if it wasn’t for Rasool Allah ﷺ kissing you, I wouldn’t have done so.

66
00:08:11,996 --> 00:08:15,963
At-Tabri(ألطبري) says; The reason why Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) made such a statement

67
00:08:17,889 --> 00:08:23,000
is because people were new to Islam and they were close to Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة).

68
00:08:24,178 --> 00:08:29,473
So he wanted to make sure that people will not revert back to the habits of Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة)

69
00:08:29,787 --> 00:08:36,230
when a rock or a stone is being kissed,

70
00:08:37,688 --> 00:08:42,866
so he wanted to make sure that they understand the reason, why he is doing that?

71
00:08:43,706 --> 00:08:45,436
Ibn Hajar(إبن حجر), he comments on this

72
00:08:45,480 --> 00:08:48,588
because this statement of Umar(عُمَر) is in Bukhari(البخاري).

73
00:08:50,427 --> 00:08:54,931
Ibn  Hajar(إبن حجر)  said: "And  this presents to us very important principle

74
00:08:55,773 --> 00:09:00,004
and that is the fact that we submit to Allahعَزّوجَلّ

75
00:09:00,948 --> 00:09:05,194
and we follow the way of Rasool Allah ﷺ, the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

76
00:09:05,597 --> 00:09:08,529
even if we don’t understand the wisdom behind it."

77
00:09:10,806 --> 00:09:15,907
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is saying; You are a stone you don’t harm you don’t benefit

78
00:09:16,535 --> 00:09:20,640
and the reason why I am kissing you is not because, I know why? I should be doing that

79
00:09:20,920 --> 00:09:23,430
it is because Rasool Allah ﷺ did that.

80
00:09:25,795 --> 00:09:27,883
So, you do it and then you ask the questions later.

81
00:09:29,829 --> 00:09:31,311
If you want to know the hikmah( حكمة)

82
00:09:31,616 --> 00:09:34,915
you are more than welcome to go and search for the hikmah( حكمة)

83
00:09:35,744 --> 00:09:38,935
but you need to do it even though you don’t know the wisdom behind it,

84
00:09:39,543 --> 00:09:42,060
and that is the ultimate level of submission.

85
00:09:42,766 --> 00:09:46,045
You submit to Allahعَزّوجَلّ even if something doesn't make a sense to you

86
00:09:46,516 --> 00:09:51,715
even if you don’t understand it, even if you don’t feel like it, even if you don’t like it,

87
00:09:52,958 --> 00:09:57,495
you do it because Allah wants you do it, and because Rasool Allah ﷺ did it.

88
00:10:00,741 --> 00:10:09,659
In fact, a lot of things are done in Hajj(حَجْ) are done without knowing the wisdom behind them

89
00:10:11,063 --> 00:10:14,211
and may be this is the reason why Hajj(حَجْ) is so special

90
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:18,511
because really Hajj(حَجْ) is the ultimate level of submitting to Allah.

91
00:10:18,551 --> 00:10:22,781
You're doing things and you don’t know the hikmah( حكمة) behind them

92
00:10:22,958 --> 00:10:26,594
but you do them, because Rasool Allah ﷺ did them and Ibrahim عليه السّلام did before him.

93
00:10:29,011 --> 00:10:33,628
Going around a building, seven times, why you are going around the Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)?

94
00:10:36,226 --> 00:10:39,597
You know now we might have these wonderful explanations that

95
00:10:41,085 --> 00:10:47,140
you go around in counter clock wise and that’s really the direction every planet revolves

96
00:10:47,513 --> 00:10:50,920
it is counter clock wise which is true.

97
00:10:52,235 --> 00:10:55,785
You would find that all of the movements in universe is counter clock wise,

98
00:10:58,391 --> 00:11:03,761
the only one, who got it wrong, is the one, who made the watch.

99
00:11:04,930 --> 00:11:06,359
They made it clock wise.

100
00:11:06,972 --> 00:11:12,169
While to be in harmony with the rest of the universe, it should be going counter clock wise.

101
00:11:12,549 --> 00:11:16,573
And that shows you that the Fitrah(فطرة) is messed up even by the one who made the watch.

102
00:11:17,947 --> 00:11:20,778
If it was a Muslim who it, they would have made it in the right direction.

103
00:11:23,025 --> 00:11:25,747
But everything in the universe is going counter clock wise

104
00:11:25,771 --> 00:11:30,437
and that is the direction you go in Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) you go counter clock wise.

105
00:11:32,957 --> 00:11:34,570
But how come you do it seven times?

106
00:11:36,082 --> 00:11:39,008
And by the way, with this explanation, the Sahabah(صحابه) didn’t know it.

107
00:11:39,098 --> 00:11:42,445
The Sahabah(صحابه) didn’t know that the planets go counter clock wise they did it

108
00:11:42,762 --> 00:11:44,485
they did it because Rasool Allah ﷺ did it.

109
00:11:44,899 --> 00:11:46,143
How come it's seven times?

110
00:11:46,167 --> 00:11:48,475
How come it's not ten or six?

111
00:11:48,570 --> 00:11:49,435
How come seven?

112
00:11:51,569 --> 00:11:55,669
You are running up and down Saffa wal Marwa(اَلصَّفَاوَلْامَروة)  just because Hajar عليها السّلام did it.

113
00:11:58,285 --> 00:12:00,690
Why is Arafah(العرفة) the greatest day?

114
00:12:00,730 --> 00:12:01,404
 What is Arafah(العرفة),

115
00:12:01,444 --> 00:12:03,232
Arafah(العرفة) is a waste land.

116
00:12:04,100 --> 00:12:11,662
It's an empty piece of land, destitude nothing grows there

117
00:12:14,791 --> 00:12:19,036
and that is the greatest day of Hajj(حَجْ), and we are just standing in land?

118
00:12:19,283 --> 00:12:22,685
Over land, it's just like any other piece of land. No different.!

119
00:12:24,864 --> 00:12:27,430
What's special about Mina(مناء), what's so special about Muzdalifah(مُذدلفه)?

120
00:12:29,777 --> 00:12:32,547
Everything that you do in Hajj(حَجْ) you doing it why?

121
00:12:32,691 --> 00:12:36,164
Just because Allah told me to do so, because Rasool Allah ﷺ did so.

122
00:12:36,888 --> 00:12:38,572
Rasool Allah ﷺ was telling the Sahabah(صحابه).

123
00:12:38,613 --> 00:12:43,122
وَاَقِفُوْاعَلى مَشَاعِرِ كُمْ فَاِنَّكُمْ عَلى اِرْثٍ مِنْ اِرِثِ اَبِيْكُمْ مِثْلِ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ

124
00:12:44,521 --> 00:12:49,833
Follow me in these rituals because you are following the way of your father Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم),

125
00:12:49,857 --> 00:12:51,936
this is the inheritance that Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) left behind.

126
00:12:55,799 --> 00:12:59,577
Kissing the black stone same thing, so what's the hikmah(حكمة) behind kissing the black stone?

127
00:12:59,601 --> 00:13:03,414
It is submission, that's what it is about.

128
00:13:03,887 --> 00:13:08,175
Submitting to Allahعَزّوجَلّ doing it, because Allah wants you to do so.

129
00:13:12,812 --> 00:13:22,766
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was very aware of the tendency of the humans to go astray

130
00:13:25,969 --> 00:13:31,034
and that’s why he was and that's why Islam is strict when it comes to following the right way.

131
00:13:32,533 --> 00:13:37,615
And you know sometimes brothers would complain when they hear the word Bida'a( بدعة)

132
00:13:37,639 --> 00:13:40,150
and you are saying everything is Bida'a( بدعة), and that is Bida'a( بدعة),

133
00:13:40,174 --> 00:13:41,919
and this is Bida'a( بدعة), no leave us alone.

134
00:13:43,113 --> 00:13:46,563
Stop telling us that everything is Bida'a( بدعة)

135
00:13:46,587 --> 00:13:48,235
everything is Bida'a(بدعة), Bida'a( بدعة), Bida'a( بدعة), Bida'a( بدعة)……..

136
00:13:49,839 --> 00:13:54,498
The thing is Islam doesn’t want to make things hard on you

137
00:13:54,657 --> 00:13:57,991
and say that everything is Bida'a(بدعة), don’t do this, don’t do that

138
00:13:59,658 --> 00:14:03,591
but there is a hikmah(حكمة) in these restrictions because

139
00:14:04,033 --> 00:14:06,977
Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) is always there and Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) wants you to go astray

140
00:14:07,001 --> 00:14:11,081
and all what Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) needs in the beginning is for you to deviate

141
00:14:11,688 --> 00:14:15,486
in a very small angle, even if it is one degree.

142
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:22,660
If you have a straight line and then he makes you deviate from that straight line one degree.

143
00:14:23,176 --> 00:14:25,359
Now, in the beginning if you draw a line

144
00:14:25,785 --> 00:14:28,532
with an angle of one degree coming out of other line

145
00:14:29,136 --> 00:14:35,693
you know you could barely distinguish the two, they are so close together that angle is so miniscule

146
00:14:36,637 --> 00:14:40,911
 but keep on going and following that line

147
00:14:41,140 --> 00:14:45,949
it will go further and further and further and further, until they are miles apart.

148
00:14:47,369 --> 00:14:51,622
So, Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) starts by getting you one step away from the straight path

149
00:14:52,290 --> 00:14:54,438
and then it just builds up from there.

150
00:14:56,340 --> 00:14:59,930
The way Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) got people into idol worshipping,

151
00:15:01,590 --> 00:15:04,169
the people were believers after Nooh(نوح).

152
00:15:04,565 --> 00:15:09,917
They followed the message of Nooh(نوح), everybody else died so the believers remained.

153
00:15:10,702 --> 00:15:15,815
When the righteous among them died, Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) came to them and said;

154
00:15:16,024 --> 00:15:20,517
Why don’t you erect statues, to remind you of As-Saliheen(ألصالحين)?

155
00:15:21,376 --> 00:15:23,692
Because remembering As-Saliheen(ألصالحين) is good for you.

156
00:15:25,462 --> 00:15:31,350
So, why don’t you have a statue for this righteous man, so that you will do good.

157
00:15:31,524 --> 00:15:35,398
You will see that statue and you will remember this good man so they liked the idea, it’s a good idea.

158
00:15:35,932 --> 00:15:41,372
 They had these statues to remind them about these pious men of the past.

159
00:15:42,178 --> 00:15:45,409
And then slowly and slowly Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) started changing their minds

160
00:15:45,763 --> 00:15:48,412
 into asking these statues.

161
00:15:48,772 --> 00:15:51,033
These are righteous men ask them to do things for you

162
00:15:51,586 --> 00:15:56,120
 and then from there, he turned them to idols that were worshipped.

163
00:15:56,329 --> 00:15:58,088
Deities worshipped besides Allah.

164
00:15:58,192 --> 00:16:04,290
Now, may be the process took centuries but he was doing it slowly but surely.

165
00:16:07,067 --> 00:16:14,505
So, Islam to close all of those gates placed these restrictions

166
00:16:15,411 --> 00:16:17,998
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) wanted to make sure that

167
00:16:18,023 --> 00:16:21,317
 no deviations would happen during his reign.

168
00:16:23,500 --> 00:16:25,582
So, for example, there was a Shajarat Ridhwan(شجرةالرضوان).

169
00:16:25,955 --> 00:16:30,954
Shajarat Ridhwan(شجرةالرضوان) is a Sidr(سدر) tree, alout tree

170
00:16:32,948 --> 00:16:36,827
where Rasool Allah ﷺ sat under this tree

171
00:16:36,851 --> 00:16:41,972
and he took the pledge of allegiance from the Sahabah(صحابه) to fight

172
00:16:43,705 --> 00:16:47,783
and the background behind that story was that Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to make Umrah(عمرة)

173
00:16:48,601 --> 00:16:50,761
and then he was prevented by the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

174
00:16:51,069 --> 00:16:54,350
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ sent a delegation, Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان).

175
00:16:55,882 --> 00:17:02,319
So, Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) he went to Makkah to meet with the leaders of Makkah

176
00:17:02,482 --> 00:17:06,557
but what happened is, he was late in coming back.

177
00:17:06,615 --> 00:17:10,294
So, there was a rumor that went around that the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) killed Uthman(عثمان).

178
00:17:11,453 --> 00:17:16,567
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ gathers the Sahabah(صحابه) and said; Pledge your allegiance to me.

179
00:17:17,086 --> 00:17:18,101
What was the pledge?

180
00:17:18,211 --> 00:17:19,591
قَالُوْا تَبَا يَعْنَ عَلى الْمَوْتَ

181
00:17:19,616 --> 00:17:20,759
We pledge to die.

182
00:17:22,457 --> 00:17:26,025
We're going to avenge for the death of Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان)

183
00:17:26,415 --> 00:17:27,979
and they pledged to die.

184
00:17:28,603 --> 00:17:31,723
Later on, it was discovered that this was a false rumor

185
00:17:32,212 --> 00:17:35,986
but that was very important point in the history of Islam

186
00:17:36,010 --> 00:17:38,989
and it is called Bay’ah-Tur-Ridhwan(بيعةالرضوان) "The Pledge of Ridhwan".

187
00:17:39,233 --> 00:17:40,282
Why is it called Ridhwan(رضوان)?

188
00:17:40,362 --> 00:17:42,219
Ridhwan(رضوان) means pleasure,

189
00:17:42,632 --> 00:17:45,929
because Allahعَزّوجَلّ was pleased with that Bay’ah(بيعة).

190
00:17:46,199 --> 00:17:48,882
Allah was pleased with the ones, who gave the Bay’ah(بيعة)

191
00:17:49,058 --> 00:17:51,343
and Allah mentions that in the Qur’an in Surah-Tul-Fath(سورة الفتح):

192
00:17:51,706 --> 00:17:55,166
لَقَدْ رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنِ الْمُؤمِنِيْنَ إِذْ يُبَايِعُوْنَكَ تَحْتَ الشَّجَر

193
00:17:56,412 --> 00:18:01,752
"Allahعَزّوجَلّ is pleased with the ones who gave you the pledge of allegiance under the tree."

194
00:18:04,029 --> 00:18:06,434
And this tree was the tree of Ridhwan(رضوان).

195
00:18:07,719 --> 00:18:13,957
In the time of Umar(عُمَر) this tree was now becoming a relic of the past.

196
00:18:14,547 --> 00:18:19,327
So, people were starting to visit it, and they would praying next to it,

197
00:18:20,393 --> 00:18:22,499
 to get Barakah(بركة) from this special location.

198
00:18:23,667 --> 00:18:27,671
So, it is an important historical site for Islam.

199
00:18:28,406 --> 00:18:33,730
This is where the pledge happened, it is very important historical site.

200
00:18:34,164 --> 00:18:35,800
What does Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) do?

201
00:18:36,443 --> 00:18:40,143
He cuts it down, he cuts down the tree.

202
00:18:45,097 --> 00:18:49,660
Now, you might be very upset because of that because you want to may be visit the tree and see it yourself

203
00:18:49,717 --> 00:18:54,164
this is where Rasool Allah ﷺ was, this is where he sat, this is where the Sahabah(صحابه) were.

204
00:18:54,496 --> 00:18:56,934
But Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) didn’t like that and he cut the tree down.

205
00:18:58,967 --> 00:18:59,284
Why?

206
00:18:59,364 --> 00:19:04,830
Because Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه didn’t want this tree to turn into an object of worship.

207
00:19:05,822 --> 00:19:08,584
 He didn’t want it to turn into an object of Barakah(بركة),

208
00:19:08,919 --> 00:19:11,049
people going and seeking Barakah(بركة) from this tree.

209
00:19:11,549 --> 00:19:19,056
 It’s a tree it doesn’t benefit, it doesn’t harm even if Rasool Allah ﷺ sat under that tree,

210
00:19:19,505 --> 00:19:21,391
it doesn’t make a difference, I am going to cut it down.

211
00:19:21,984 --> 00:19:25,228
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was farthest being sentimental person.

212
00:19:26,990 --> 00:19:34,609
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), his logic and common sense and mind would take over his emotions.

213
00:19:35,582 --> 00:19:39,610
The Sahabah(صحابه) would have great emotions to this location because they were there.

214
00:19:40,887 --> 00:19:44,823
They were the ones, who gave Bay’ah(بيعة) to Rasool Ullahﷺ there, Umar(عُمَر) was one of them.

215
00:19:45,665 --> 00:19:50,954
So, they must have had extremely strong emotional attachment to that location.

216
00:19:51,384 --> 00:19:55,726
It brings back the wonderful memory of Bay’ah-Tur-Ridhwan(بيعةالرضوان)

217
00:19:56,229 --> 00:19:58,451
but Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) would not think about that

218
00:19:58,490 --> 00:20:02,418
he is thinking about the implications, he is thinking about the future, so he cuts down the tree.

219
00:20:05,047 --> 00:20:11,304
In another incident, he saw men praying in a particular location, they were praying.

220
00:20:12,375 --> 00:20:14,201
He said: How come you are praying here?

221
00:20:14,320 --> 00:20:16,042
They said: Rasool Allah ﷺ prayed here.

222
00:20:16,414 --> 00:20:20,250
He said: If it’s a time for Salah(صلاة) pray anywhere otherwise you leave.

223
00:20:22,218 --> 00:20:27,029
And then he said: What has destroyed the people before you

224
00:20:27,407 --> 00:20:32,028
is when they have taken the places of their Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) as places of worship.

225
00:20:33,299 --> 00:20:37,672
The place where the Nabi(نَبِي) prayers or place where Nabi(نَبِي) dies, they take the place as a worship.

226
00:20:37,791 --> 00:20:39,014
 He said: That destroyed them.

227
00:20:44,252 --> 00:20:46,934
With the grave of Daniyal(دانيال).

228
00:20:47,255 --> 00:20:55,592
Daniyal(دانيال), Daniel in the Bible is a Prophet that is not mentioned in the Qur’an

229
00:20:55,734 --> 00:20:57,334
and is not mentioned in Sunnah(سنة).

230
00:20:58,448 --> 00:21:06,063
We don’t have any textual reference that Daniyal(دانيال) is a Prophet.

231
00:21:08,030 --> 00:21:10,033
In Arabic it is referred to as Daniyal(دانيال).

232
00:21:12,210 --> 00:21:17,192
However, in the Bible Daniel is a prophet

233
00:21:18,571 --> 00:21:23,419
and there is a book of Daniel and it talks about the events of end of time.

234
00:21:26,886 --> 00:21:33,663
The Ahadith(احاديث) of Fittan(فتن), the Christians are attributed to Daniel.

235
00:21:39,211 --> 00:21:43,691
His grave or what the people claimed to be his grave was uncovered.

236
00:21:45,914 --> 00:21:51,341
And what made the Muslims think that Daniyal(دانيال) is actually a Nabi(نَبِي),

237
00:21:52,252 --> 00:21:55,912
is when they saw that the earth has not affected his body.

238
00:21:58,298 --> 00:22:02,050
The Muslim opened the land of Tastur(تستر) in the time of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب)

239
00:22:02,075 --> 00:22:06,383
and that is when the flood uncovered the grave of Daniel.

240
00:22:08,739 --> 00:22:12,983
And they saw his body intact with no scratches at all.

241
00:22:14,023 --> 00:22:16,372
And we know that Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

242
00:22:17,209 --> 00:22:20,964
اِنَّ اللهَ حَرَّمَ عَلَى الْاَرْضَ، اَنْ تَأْكُلَ اَجْسَا دَالْاَنْبِيَاءََ

243
00:22:21,835 --> 00:22:26,849
Allah has prevented the earth from eating the bodies of the prophets.

244
00:22:27,666 --> 00:22:33,806
So, they said, most likely this man was a prophet because he had died hundreds of year ago

245
00:22:34,072 --> 00:22:35,213
 and his body is still intact.

246
00:22:38,288 --> 00:22:40,021
So, now they have to rebury him.

247
00:22:40,728 --> 00:22:42,235
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) sends a letter,

248
00:22:42,376 --> 00:22:44,879
see Umar(عُمَر) is thinking about the implications of that.

249
00:22:46,650 --> 00:22:52,369
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه sends a letter and he said,

250
00:22:53,400 --> 00:23:02,273
in bright light during day time, I want you to dig thirteen graves in different areas

251
00:23:04,468 --> 00:23:07,090
and then under the cover of darkness

252
00:23:07,538 --> 00:23:12,055
you go and burry the body of Daniyal(دانيال) without anybody seeing you

253
00:23:12,765 --> 00:23:16,369
and you cover up all the graves at once.

254
00:23:17,990 --> 00:23:19,462
Why Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) do that?

255
00:23:19,959 --> 00:23:23,500
So, that he would confuse the people they would not know which one is his grave.

256
00:23:24,779 --> 00:23:28,217
Dig thirteen graves during the day time, so people know the locations.

257
00:23:28,638 --> 00:23:36,387
At night you burry him, you cover up all the graves people now don’t know which one is the grave of Daniyal(دانيال).

258
00:23:37,148 --> 00:23:37,397
Why?

259
00:23:37,484 --> 00:23:40,535
Because he didn’t want that grave to be worshiped.

260
00:23:48,703 --> 00:23:50,132
With Khalid Ibn Waleed(خالد ابن وليد),

261
00:23:50,836 --> 00:23:53,713
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) he fires Khalid Ibn Waleed(خالد ابن وليد).

262
00:23:55,015 --> 00:23:58,451
That’s one of the first orders of the Al-Khalifah(الخليفه).

263
00:24:01,127 --> 00:24:10,664
Khalid Ibn Waleed(خالد ابن وليد) relinquishes all of his authorities as a military leader

264
00:24:11,130 --> 00:24:17,220
and he immediately and suddenly turns into becoming a regular soldier.

265
00:24:20,505 --> 00:24:25,795
So, the people were wondering why did the Khalifah(خليفه) do that?

266
00:24:25,819 --> 00:24:28,865
I mean, Khalid Ibn Waleed(خالد ابن وليد) was such an impressive leader.

267
00:24:29,506 --> 00:24:38,447
Khalid Ibn Waleed(خالد ابن وليد), dear brothers and sisters, never in his life, ever he never lost a battle

268
00:24:40,282 --> 00:24:42,552
 in Islam and in Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة).

269
00:24:44,731 --> 00:24:49,071
Every battle that he lead in Islam or before Islam, he won.

270
00:24:50,489 --> 00:24:51,989
He never lost

271
00:24:53,537 --> 00:25:00,326
and he had skills and we talked about some of these when we were talking about Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

272
00:25:00,943 --> 00:25:02,243
He was like a storm,

273
00:25:03,177 --> 00:25:10,011
who just go around from one part of the land to another and they would say:

274
00:25:10,036 --> 00:25:12,346
لَا يَنَامْ وَلَايَتْرُكْ اَحَدًا يَنَامْ

275
00:25:13,014 --> 00:25:15,979
He would not sleep and would not anybody else to sleep.

276
00:25:17,295 --> 00:25:21,499
He would not sleep himself and he would not let friend or foe, sleep.

277
00:25:22,183 --> 00:25:23,350
And it was like a hurricane.

278
00:25:24,894 --> 00:25:31,225
And he had such a swift movement from one battle ground to another that he drives his enemy crazy.

279
00:25:31,589 --> 00:25:34,130
They try to plan him out Khalid Ibn Waleed(خالد ابن وليد) is here, okay let's plan

280
00:25:34,470 --> 00:25:35,645
suddenly, he is somewhere else.

281
00:25:35,708 --> 00:25:37,573
They plan, suddenly he is somewhere else

282
00:25:37,829 --> 00:25:39,028
So, he just drove them crazy.

283
00:25:39,829 --> 00:25:56,605
In fact when the Muslims were sending urgent messages to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to send reinforcements to them in Ash-Sham(ألشام).

284
00:25:58,148 --> 00:26:00,405
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) sends a letter to Khalid Ibn Waleed(خالد ابن وليد),

285
00:26:00,430 --> 00:26:04,359
who was in Iraq and told him to go and rescue the Muslims in Ash-Sham(ألشام).

286
00:26:06,546 --> 00:26:14,912
Now, the Roman had garrisons all over the known routes of travel between Al-Iraq and Ash-Sham(ألشام).

287
00:26:16,242 --> 00:26:22,353
Suddenly out of nowhere Khalid Ibn Waleed رضي الله عنه and the Muslim army show up in the middle of Ash-Sham(ألشام).

288
00:26:23,929 --> 00:26:25,215
The Roman said; Where did he come from?

289
00:26:25,286 --> 00:26:28,612
All of the roads are protected with the garrisons.

290
00:26:29,187 --> 00:26:36,272
Khalid Ibn Waleed(خالد ابن وليد) has traveled through desert land, which was never ever travelled before him.

291
00:26:37,042 --> 00:26:40,655
It was the first time ever an army has crossed that desert

292
00:26:41,831 --> 00:26:44,858
and he suddenly lands right in the center of Ash-Sham(ألشام),

293
00:26:45,989 --> 00:26:49,532
by passing all of the Roman security points.

294
00:26:51,966 --> 00:26:54,000
And now, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) fires him,

295
00:26:55,238 --> 00:26:57,666
so Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

296
00:26:58,254 --> 00:27:02,115
اِنِّيْ لَمْ اَعْزِلْ خالد ابن وليد اَنْ سَخْطَه وَلَا خِيَانَةْ

297
00:27:03,039 --> 00:27:09,099
وَلَكِنَّ النَاَسَ فُتِنُوْا بِهِ فَاَحْبَبْتُ اَنْ يَعْلَمُوْ اَنَّ الله هُوَّالثَّانِعْء

298
00:27:10,392 --> 00:27:18,902
I didn’t not fire Khalid Ibn Waleed رضي الله عنه because I am angry with him,

299
00:27:19,215 --> 00:27:24,351
or because of betrayal of trust, or responsibility,

300
00:27:25,232 --> 00:27:26,986
but the reason was,

301
00:27:27,502 --> 00:27:31,067
that he was becoming a Fitnah(فِتْنَه) for the people.

302
00:27:32,025 --> 00:27:35,841
And I wanted the people to know that it is Allah, Who gives victory.

303
00:27:37,650 --> 00:27:42,861
People were attributing victory to the person of Khalid(خالد).

304
00:27:43,756 --> 00:27:49,265
It is Khalid(خالد), who is making us these victories, he is the one creating them.

305
00:27:50,646 --> 00:27:53,169
So, Umar(عُمَر) said; He was turning into a Fitnah(فِتْنَه) for the people.

306
00:27:53,193 --> 00:27:54,790
They were attributing that to him.

307
00:27:55,231 --> 00:27:57,430
When it should be attributed to Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

308
00:27:57,692 --> 00:28:02,779
So, he wanted the people to know that victory comes from Allah and that victory will carry on

309
00:28:03,183 --> 00:28:07,784
even when somebody else assumes responsibility and that was true.

310
00:28:08,409 --> 00:28:10,377
The Muslims carried on wining.

311
00:28:15,811 --> 00:28:20,658
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was fighting false ideas or assumptions.

312
00:28:22,529 --> 00:28:25,267
He saw some men from Yemen, who were traveling

313
00:28:27,123 --> 00:28:29,639
and again they are part of those people which we said,

314
00:28:29,888 --> 00:28:32,128
you know they just do nothing just walk lazily.

315
00:28:33,930 --> 00:28:36,414
So, Umar(عُمَر) said: Who are these?

316
00:28:36,898 --> 00:28:37,601
They said;

317
00:28:37,829 --> 00:28:42,310
هَااُؤلآءِ الْمُتَّوَكِلُوْنَ

318
00:28:42,438 --> 00:28:45,959
These are the one who have Tawakkul(توكل) in Allah, so they don’t work.

319
00:28:46,419 --> 00:28:50,571
They just have Tawakul(توكل), they don’t work, they have Tawakul(توكل) in Allah.

320
00:28:51,654 --> 00:28:59,302
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) went to them with the "Durrah(درَّة)" and he said;

321
00:29:00,905 --> 00:29:03,307
بَلْ هُمْ اَلْمُتَوَا كِلُوْنَ

322
00:29:04,350 --> 00:29:08,778
They are the ones, who are dependent "Mutawaaqil(متواكل)" means dependent,

323
00:29:09,900 --> 00:29:15,852
the Mutawaqqil(متوكل) is the one who plants his seed and then puts his trusts in Allah.

324
00:29:17,415 --> 00:29:23,150
So, you have to plant the seed first than after that you leave results to Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

325
00:29:28,357 --> 00:29:31,434
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) did not want to deal with the society of bumps.

326
00:29:32,352 --> 00:29:34,637
He wanted the people to work, to be productive.

327
00:29:40,695 --> 00:29:43,788
This man comes from Faris(فارس), Persia,

328
00:29:46,077 --> 00:29:48,014
delivering good news to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب).

329
00:29:48,039 --> 00:29:51,237
He said; We opened Al-Madayan(مدائن), Al-Madayan(مدائن) was the capital of Persia,

330
00:29:53,405 --> 00:29:59,788
he said and we found a book that has wonderful words.

331
00:30:03,296 --> 00:30:06,399
They found this book and it has so much wisdom in it.

332
00:30:08,415 --> 00:30:09,605
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

333
00:30:09,839 --> 00:30:11,226
اَمِنْ كِتَابِ اللهِ هُوَ؟

334
00:30:13,887 --> 00:30:15,968
Are these words are from the book of Allah?

335
00:30:16,941 --> 00:30:17,829
He said: No,

336
00:30:18,940 --> 00:30:23,868
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) started beating him with the Durrah(درَّة).

337
00:30:24,693 --> 00:30:28,895
By the way, brothers don’t think that it’s a huge baton or stick, cane that he is carrying,

338
00:30:29,172 --> 00:30:32,862
 it’s a small stick it’s a more of symbolic thing.

339
00:30:33,935 --> 00:30:38,401
It's not a physical beating, it's of a symbolic nature.

340
00:30:39,060 --> 00:30:41,471
So, he would actually tap the people.

341
00:30:42,865 --> 00:30:48,488
I don’t want you to get wrong impression also when I talk about Umar(عُمَر) being severe,

342
00:30:48,797 --> 00:30:51,378
I don’t want you going around being severe with people

343
00:30:51,897 --> 00:30:55,987
to reenact what you think is Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب).

344
00:30:56,210 --> 00:30:57,877
That was Shiddah(شدة) in the right place.

345
00:30:57,902 --> 00:31:02,825
That was a toughness used in the right way in the right place.

346
00:31:04,021 --> 00:31:08,443
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) assumed responsibility at a time when the Ummah(امة) needed that.

347
00:31:09,608 --> 00:31:12,497
In the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ that would have been inappropriate,

348
00:31:12,521 --> 00:31:15,950
and that is why the personality of the Rasool Allah ﷺ was soft and compassionate.

349
00:31:16,813 --> 00:31:20,403
Because that was in time of Da'wah(دعوة), people needed to be attracted.

350
00:31:20,427 --> 00:31:23,179
وَلَوْكُنْتَ فَظَّاغَلِيْظَ الْقَلْبِ لَا نْفَضُّوْ امِنْ حَوْلِكْ

351
00:31:23,722 --> 00:31:29,194
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says: "If you were severe and hard natured people would have abandoned you."

352
00:31:30,011 --> 00:31:34,100
But Umar(عُمَر) became Khalifah(خليفه) in times when Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) was opening up on the Muslims.

353
00:31:34,706 --> 00:31:37,523
So, there was a potential of a huge problem,

354
00:31:37,824 --> 00:31:42,532
Muslims being attached to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and their hearts becoming greedy.

355
00:31:42,814 --> 00:31:47,748
So, they needed somebody stern and firm to keep them on the straight path.

356
00:31:51,506 --> 00:31:56,057
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) he was tapping this man with the Durrah(درَّة)

357
00:31:57,178 --> 00:32:00,455
