532
00:46:00,478 --> 00:46:04,449
"لَوْ خَشِعَ قَلْبَ هَذَا لَخَشِعَتْ جَوَارِهُ"

533
00:46:06,625 --> 00:46:08,931
UMAR IBN KHATTAB WAS A MAN OF Dua(دُعَا)

534
00:46:10,710 --> 00:46:12,980
إِذَااَبْطَعَتْ عَلَيْهِ جُيُوْشَ قَنَتْ

535
00:46:13,835 --> 00:46:22,744
It's narrated that when the news of the armies would be late, he would make Qunoot(قنوت).

536
00:46:23,818 --> 00:46:26,815
And when the armies  would be late in coming back, he would make Qunoot(قنوت).

537
00:46:27,123 --> 00:46:27,915
Qunoot(قنوت) is Dua(دُعَا).

538
00:46:30,185 --> 00:46:34,643
He was very concerned, he was very concerned with the state of the Ummah(امة) especially

539
00:46:35,091 --> 00:46:38,132
the Ghazu(غزؤ) that concerned him a lot.

540
00:46:38,221 --> 00:46:41,955
The Ghazu(غزؤ) and the Financial situation of the Muslims.

541
00:46:44,083 --> 00:46:46,400
With all of this Khushu(خشوع) that Umar(عُمَر) had

542
00:46:46,734 --> 00:46:52,038
it is narrated that he once,  woke up to pray Salaat At-Tahajjud(صلاة التهجد)

543
00:46:56,069 --> 00:46:58,130
and he couldn’t have concentration in the Salah(صلاة).

544
00:46:59,058 --> 00:47:01,325
So, he went to sleep, he couldn’t sleep.

545
00:47:03,041 --> 00:47:09,831
And then he said; When I pray, I cannot pray and when I try to sleep, I cannot sleep.

546
00:47:10,281 --> 00:47:14,339
So, they asked him why, He said: Because I am concerned about my people.

547
00:47:16,414 --> 00:47:21,203
He is thinking so much about the Muslims, he couldn’t pray and he couldn’t sleep.

548
00:47:22,885 --> 00:47:25,340
So, he was very concerned with the Ummah(امة).

549
00:47:25,557 --> 00:47:27,943
We ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to give us leaders who are concerned,

550
00:47:28,861 --> 00:47:30,081
who have care for the Ummah(امة).

551
00:47:30,836 --> 00:47:33,848
And the Ummah(امة) is now like a flock without a Sheppard,

552
00:47:36,809 --> 00:47:39,385
surrounded with wolves from every direction.

553
00:47:39,806 --> 00:47:40,949
 Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) says;

554
00:47:41,499 --> 00:47:48,635
وَكَانَ يَدْعُوْ الِلْمُجَاهِدِيْنَ فِيْ صَلَوتِهِ وَيَقْنُتْ لِيْ ذَلِكْ فَاعِنْدَ مَا قَتَلَ اَهْلِ الْكِتَابْ قَنَعْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ فِي الصَّلَوةِ  الْمَكْتُوْبَةَ

555
00:47:49,327 --> 00:47:51,877
He used to pray to make Dua(دُعَا) for the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) in his Salah(صلاة)

556
00:47:52,553 --> 00:47:54,337
and he would make Dua(دُعَا) Al-Qunoot(قنوت) for that,

557
00:47:54,810 --> 00:47:56,571
and when he fought against the people of the Book

558
00:47:56,595 --> 00:47:59,474
he would make a Dua(دُعَا) against the people of the Book he would say; O Allah,

559
00:47:59,880 --> 00:48:03,744
اَللَّهُمَّ عَلَيْكَ بِالْكَفَرَ مِنْ اَهْلِ الْكِتَابْ

560
00:48:03,769 --> 00:48:08,050
O Allah! Destroy the disbelievers, of the people of the Book.

561
00:48:10,460 --> 00:48:14,128
And this is when he is fighting against the Roman Empire.

562
00:48:15,725 --> 00:48:18,608
And he used to make Qunoot(قنوت) against them in Salah(صلاة) of Fard(فرض),

563
00:48:19,014 --> 00:48:20,932
in Fajr(فجر), Dhuhar(ظهر), Asr(عصر), Maghrib(مغرب) and Ishaa(عشاء).

564
00:48:21,508 --> 00:48:24,607
He would make the Dua(دُعَا) against the people of the Book.

565
00:48:30,306 --> 00:48:34,376
AND JUMAA(جمعه), KHALIFA(خليفه) WANTED PEOPLE TO BE ON TIME;

566
00:48:37,660 --> 00:48:43,105
He started giving Khutbah(خطبه) and here comes Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان),

567
00:48:44,082 --> 00:48:45,220
walking into the Masjid(مسجد).

568
00:48:46,313 --> 00:48:50,359
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) in front of everyone he stops his Khutbah(خطبه) and he said;

569
00:48:50,493 --> 00:48:51,660
أَفِيْ هَذِهِ سَّاعَةْ؟

570
00:48:52,750 --> 00:48:53,860
Is this, when you show up?

571
00:48:55,938 --> 00:49:04,539
Uthman Ibn Affan رضى الله عنه said: I was so busy and I only went back home now

572
00:49:04,997 --> 00:49:06,597
and I made Wudu(وضؤ) and came

573
00:49:06,929 --> 00:49:09,711
and he said: And you are also telling me that, you only made Wudu(وضؤ),

574
00:49:10,109 --> 00:49:13,101
when you know that Rasool Allah ﷺ use to tell us that we need to make Ghusal(غسل).

575
00:49:15,755 --> 00:49:21,735
So, he wanted people to be on time and follow the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

576
00:49:22,661 --> 00:49:25,855
Don’t be late to Salaat-Ul-Juma(صلاة الجمعه),

577
00:49:25,880 --> 00:49:28,497
you need to be there before Imam(اِمَام) starts the Khuttab(خطبه).

578
00:49:35,128 --> 00:49:42,689
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) even though he didn’t want his wives to pray in the Masjid(مسجد)

579
00:49:43,354 --> 00:49:47,379
but he didn’t prevent them, because of the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

580
00:49:47,464 --> 00:49:49,554
لَا تَمْنَعُ عِمَا اللهَ مَسَاجِدَاللهَ

581
00:49:49,961 --> 00:49:54,634
Don’t prevent the women servants of Allah, from praying in the Houses of Allah.

582
00:49:55,623 --> 00:49:59,494
So, he told his wife, You know my preference,

583
00:50:00,180 --> 00:50:03,932
she said: "I am not going to stop going to the Masjid(مسجد) until you tell me to do so".

584
00:50:04,141 --> 00:50:12,107
She knows that he won’t and she carried on praying in the Masjid(مسجد)

585
00:50:12,229 --> 00:50:16,162
and in Bukhari(بخاريْ) it says that, when he was stabbed in Salah(صلاة) and killed,

586
00:50:16,713 --> 00:50:17,738
she was in the Masjid(مسجد).

587
00:50:19,112 --> 00:50:21,283
When Umar(عُمَر) was assassinated in the Salaat-Ul-Fajr(صلاة الفجر),

588
00:50:21,553 --> 00:50:26,089
she was in the Masjid(مسجد), so she carried on praying until he died in the Masjid(مسجد).

589
00:50:26,522 --> 00:50:27,283
He didn’t prevent her.

590
00:50:29,617 --> 00:50:32,084
NOW I NEED TO MAKE A COMMENT ON THAT;

591
00:50:32,144 --> 00:50:39,434
In those days it would be alright to tell the woman to pray at home

592
00:50:40,587 --> 00:50:50,111
because in Madina, they would find benefit at home, they would find benefit on the streets

593
00:50:50,135 --> 00:50:55,463
they would find benefit in the Masjid(مسجد), I mean it's all an Islamic Society.

594
00:50:56,736 --> 00:51:04,298
However, now a days, for those brothers, who do not want their women to pray in the Masjid(مسجد)

595
00:51:05,798 --> 00:51:07,540
 and you tell them that, that’s your preference

596
00:51:07,564 --> 00:51:11,679
first of you can say that it's your preference but you cannot prevent them.

597
00:51:12,138 --> 00:51:14,002
You do not have the right to prevent them.

598
00:51:14,529 --> 00:51:18,450
Because of the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ do not prevent them from going to the Masjid(مسجد).

599
00:51:19,180 --> 00:51:25,442
And if you make that your preference known to them and they agree to stay,

600
00:51:26,093 --> 00:51:30,218
 you are responsible you need to provide them with an alternative.

601
00:51:30,704 --> 00:51:33,655
You need to provide them with the services that they would get in the Masjid(مسجد).

602
00:51:35,130 --> 00:51:38,827
You can’t just tell your wife or daughter to stay home alright

603
00:51:39,145 --> 00:51:41,954
and then leave her with the TV Set to be her Shaikh(شيخ).

604
00:51:43,684 --> 00:51:45,378
You have to offer her an alternative.

605
00:51:47,288 --> 00:51:50,438
Preventing women from going to the Masajid(مساجد) today,

606
00:51:51,152 --> 00:51:55,266
if there is Ilm(علم) and Islamic Activities that they would learn from the Masjid(مسجد)

607
00:51:55,746 --> 00:52:03,618
is not a wise idea if you are not going to offer them with a viable Islamic program.

608
00:52:05,478 --> 00:52:10,770
So may be the recommendation now should be that for benefit,

609
00:52:11,570 --> 00:52:12,718
if there is benefit in the Masjid(مسجد)

610
00:52:12,758 --> 00:52:15,256
because in some Masajid(مساجد) there is no benefit, you just do the Salah(صلاة) and leave.

611
00:52:15,336 --> 00:52:19,351
I mean the Masjid(مسجد) is dead.

612
00:52:21,448 --> 00:52:27,111
You know, you finish the Salah(صلاة) and then the person who has the keys, the care-taker of the Masjid(مسجد)

613
00:52:28,079 --> 00:52:31,072
he is shaking the keys next to you, it's time to leave brother.!

614
00:52:31,452 --> 00:52:33,990
Time to leave! And he is ringing those keys

615
00:52:35,506 --> 00:52:39,149
and turning off the lights. Yullah, Yullah out!.

616
00:52:40,612 --> 00:52:41,984
So, the Masjid(مسجد) is dead

617
00:52:43,018 --> 00:52:53,259
but if there is an activity going on there is Halaqat(حلقات) of Ilm(علم) there is something that would benefit our Muslim sister

618
00:52:53,665 --> 00:52:59,361
 then she should go and she should be encouraged to go to Masajid(مساجد).

619
00:53:00,369 --> 00:53:03,623
It doesn’t make a sense to allow her everywhere except the Masjid(مسجد),

620
00:53:06,080 --> 00:53:10,608
you can go to school, you can go to university, you can go shopping, you can here and there,

621
00:53:10,826 --> 00:53:14,123
you can go visit your family but you are not allowed to go to Masjid(مسجد).

622
00:53:15,217 --> 00:53:16,581
No the Masjid(مسجد) is for men.

623
00:53:25,899 --> 00:53:28,573
Sister leave the Takbir(تكبير) to the brothers. I guess!!

624
00:53:31,801 --> 00:53:35,144
Brothers you should do the Takbir(تكبير) for the sisters! Do the Takbir(تكبير) for them,

625
00:53:36,151 --> 00:53:39,347
Audience: Takbir(تكبير)!! Allah Akbar(الله اكبر), Takbir(تكبير)!! Allah Akbar(الله اكبر), Takbir(تكبير)!!

626
00:53:39,372 --> 00:53:43,569
Allah Akbar(الله اكبر), Takbir(تكبير)!! Allah Akbar(الله اكبر) , Takbir(تكبير)!! Allah Akbar(الله اكبر).

627
00:53:43,947 --> 00:53:48,213
So sisters, should be very happy that this is the first time ever that we have Five Takbir(تكبير)'s.

628
00:53:48,965 --> 00:53:53,293
So, ya’ni(يعني), this brother must be a champion of women rights

629
00:53:53,608 --> 00:53:55,188
Ma sha Allah(ماشاءالله)

630
00:53:56,411 --> 00:53:57,859
Ma sha Allah(ماشاءالله), Jazakallahu khairun(جزاك الله خيرًا ) brother.

631
00:53:58,199 --> 00:54:00,265
I am sure that's not the case you are just a bachelor

632
00:54:03,402 --> 00:54:05,573
trying to develop a good reputation for yourself.

633
00:54:21,750 --> 00:54:29,277
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه would sometimes go to his friend Abu Musa Al-Ashari(أبو موسى ألأشعري)

634
00:54:29,317 --> 00:54:32,001
all of them were friends, the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, brothers.

635
00:54:33,523 --> 00:54:39,122
You know this is one thing, if you never experience brotherhood

636
00:54:39,602 --> 00:54:42,077
it's something that cannot be expressed in words.

637
00:54:42,540 --> 00:54:45,513
Al-Akhuwah Fillah(الاخواةفى الله) brotherhood for the sake of Allah

638
00:54:46,212 --> 00:54:51,853
is such a wonderful blessing of Allah in this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) it cannot be described in words,

639
00:54:52,355 --> 00:54:54,228
 it’s a blessings straight out of Jannah(جنة).

640
00:54:56,871 --> 00:55:02,997
And these Sahabah(صحابه) had it, and this brotherhood is not something that you develop through casual relationships.

641
00:55:04,318 --> 00:55:12,972
Usually this is a relationship that develops when they go through similar experiences of hardship.

642
00:55:14,979 --> 00:55:19,214
So, the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم had it because they were tortured together.

643
00:55:20,362 --> 00:55:22,514
They fought in the same Trench together,

644
00:55:23,651 --> 00:55:25,713
they suffered hunger together.

645
00:55:26,470 --> 00:55:32,426
You know you remember the story, when Rasool Allah ﷺ went out of his house and he meets Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

646
00:55:32,481 --> 00:55:37,544
 and he said: Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) why are you walking in the streets at this late hour?

647
00:55:37,859 --> 00:55:41,347
He said, O Rasool Ullah because I am hungry, I am going to search for food.

648
00:55:41,680 --> 00:55:45,507
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: This is the same reason why, I am out

649
00:55:46,017 --> 00:55:48,549
and then they met Umar(عُمَر) and the same thing he said.

650
00:55:48,731 --> 00:55:50,222
So, they suffered together.

651
00:55:53,119 --> 00:55:57,131
And that’s how they develop the strong bonding.

652
00:55:58,436 --> 00:56:01,709
And then because of the battles that, they fought

653
00:56:02,576 --> 00:56:07,002
being soldiers who are together that also develops the special relationship between them.

654
00:56:08,509 --> 00:56:11,684
You would even find that between the soldiers who are non Muslims.

655
00:56:12,679 --> 00:56:17,869
You know that experience of being together at that moment of danger develops a special bonding.

656
00:56:18,500 --> 00:56:22,207
So, the Sahabah(صحابه) in addition to having that, they also had Akhuwah Fillah(الاخواةفى الله)

657
00:56:22,232 --> 00:56:23,934
the brotherhood for the sake of Allahعَزّوجَلّ

658
00:56:24,172 --> 00:56:26,448
you know it's not just the experience of fighting together

659
00:56:26,485 --> 00:56:32,969
but it's also the love for the sake of Allah, Emaan(إيمان) having the same goals in life,

660
00:56:33,442 --> 00:56:39,928
working for the same cause, their relationshipwas very tight, very tight.

661
00:56:43,035 --> 00:56:46,271
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه, sometimes, would come to Abu Musa Al-Asha'ri(أبو موسى ألأشعري)

662
00:56:47,227 --> 00:56:50,062
and he would tell him Abu Musa(أبوموسى) start reciting for us.

663
00:56:51,285 --> 00:56:54,709
So, Abu Musa Al-Asha'ri(أبو موسى ألأشعري) would recite Ayaat(آيات) from Qur’an

664
00:56:55,183 --> 00:56:58,444
and then they would all cry, they would all cry together.

665
00:57:00,487 --> 00:57:07,571
Once the servant of Usayd(أسيد) his slave, he is the one narrating this, he said:

666
00:57:07,902 --> 00:57:15,547
He said: Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) used to patrol at night, and we'll talk about his patrols

667
00:57:15,830 --> 00:57:20,190
 tomorrow night In Sha Allah Ta'ala(إن شاء لله تعالى), his nightly patrols.

668
00:57:23,166 --> 00:57:30,445
So, he would go to the Masjid(مسجد) and he would prevent anyone from staying in the Masjid(مسجد)

669
00:57:31,486 --> 00:57:33,388
except the ones who are praying.

670
00:57:34,337 --> 00:57:36,849
He didn’t want people hanging around the Masjid(مسجد) after Ishaa(عشاء).

671
00:57:37,875 --> 00:57:41,348
After Ishaa(عشاء) you go back home unless you are praying.

672
00:57:41,860 --> 00:57:43,622
Don’t just sit around in Masjid(مسجد), talking.

673
00:57:45,984 --> 00:57:49,852
So, he was going around Masjid(مسجد) he came and he saw this Halaqah(حلقه) he said,

674
00:57:49,973 --> 00:57:51,668
who are they? They said:

675
00:57:51,708 --> 00:57:52,882
"إِنَّمَا هُمْ اَهْلُكْ"

676
00:57:53,758 --> 00:57:54,852
It is your family.

677
00:57:55,890 --> 00:57:58,461
Actually there were none of the relatives of Umar(عُمَر) there.

678
00:57:59,175 --> 00:58:03,952
These were some his close Sahabah(صحابه) his brothers, he said, Ah-luk(أهلُك) your family.

679
00:58:05,228 --> 00:58:06,302
I mean your family.

680
00:58:07,315 --> 00:58:14,810
So, he goes there and he sits down with them, and he said,

681
00:58:15,286 --> 00:58:17,258
why are you staying behind the Salah(صلاة)? They said:

682
00:58:17,289 --> 00:58:18,949
جَلَسْنَا نَذْكُرَالله عزًوْجل

683
00:58:19,625 --> 00:58:22,838
We are sitting to remember Allahعزوجل.

684
00:58:22,990 --> 00:58:24,248
So, he sat down with them.

685
00:58:24,624 --> 00:58:26,868
When he knew that he is making Zikr(ذكر) of Allah, he sat down with them.

686
00:58:28,031 --> 00:58:29,820
and then he told the one next to him:

687
00:58:30,464 --> 00:58:31,179
ادنهم له

688
00:58:31,204 --> 00:58:33,508
The one, who is right next to him, He said;

689
00:58:34,411 --> 00:58:35,250
خُذْ فِى الدُّعَاء

690
00:58:35,621 --> 00:58:36,677
Make Dua(دُعَا) for us.

691
00:58:37,817 --> 00:58:39,224
So, the man started making Dua(دُعَا)

692
00:58:39,871 --> 00:58:44,159
and then Umar(عُمَر) would go around asking everyone to make Dua(دُعَا) for the group

693
00:58:44,671 --> 00:58:45,510
 and they would say Ameen(آمين).

694
00:58:46,951 --> 00:58:49,394
Until he gets, to this servant, the slave,

695
00:58:50,931 --> 00:58:52,869
and he said: You make Dua(دُعَا) for us now

696
00:58:55,529 --> 00:58:58,635
and I was the last one before him, He said;

697
00:58:59,245 --> 00:59:00,875
"فَأُحْصِرْتْ"

698
00:59:01,279 --> 00:59:02,314
I couldn't speak,

699
00:59:03,811 --> 00:59:05,039
وَأَخَذْتُ اَفْقُلَ

700
00:59:05,807 --> 00:59:07,814
And I was shaking.

701
00:59:09,031 --> 00:59:13,575
This is an unlearned man, he is not used to speaking in front of people

702
00:59:14,626 --> 00:59:16,596
and he didn't know what to say.

703
00:59:17,259 --> 00:59:20,376
So, he couldn’t speak.

704
00:59:22,597 --> 00:59:27,202
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told him say anything even if you say,

705
00:59:27,226 --> 00:59:29,297
اَللَّهُمَ اغْفِرْلَنَا اَللَّهُمَ اَرْحَمْ لَنَا

706
00:59:30,902 --> 00:59:33,249
O Allaah! Forgive us O Allaah! Have a mercy on us.

707
00:59:33,759 --> 00:59:35,916
Just say something, make a Dua(دُعَا) for us anything.

708
00:59:36,576 --> 00:59:41,009
It doesn’t have to be a long sophisticated Dua(دُعَا) that you memorize out of a book,

709
00:59:41,482 --> 00:59:43,094
anything, make any Dua(دُعَا).

710
00:59:44,025 --> 00:59:47,870
And I'll come back to this.

711
00:59:48,401 --> 00:59:54,555
So, he said: I said those words, and then it was Umar(عُمَر)’s turn to make Dua(دُعَا)

712
00:59:55,049 --> 01:00:02,543
and he made Dua(دُعَا) and he was the one, who was crying the most among us and then he said:

713
01:00:02,568 --> 01:00:03,598
اَلْآنَ فَتَفَرَّقُو

714
01:00:03,810 --> 01:00:05,087
Now everybody go home.

715
01:00:09,334 --> 01:00:11,388
With the word of Umar(عُمَر) make any Dua(دُعَا),

716
01:00:11,752 --> 01:00:14,513
you know you see people in Tawaf(طواف),

717
01:00:15,376 --> 01:00:19,353
if you have been to Hajj(حَجْ) or Umrah(عمرة) reading form these booklets.

718
01:00:21,108 --> 01:00:23,307
There is Dua(دُعَا) that you say in first Tawaf(طواف),

719
01:00:23,430 --> 01:00:24,786
Dua(دُعَا) that you say that in second,

720
01:00:24,837 --> 01:00:27,074
Dua(دُعَا) that you say in third, Dua(دُعَا) in the fourth,

721
01:00:27,703 --> 01:00:31,371
then they have the book for Saffa(ألصفا) and Marwa(مروة), they have book for everything.

722
01:00:33,570 --> 01:00:38,566
And they are reading for this book and they are bumping into people because they cannot see.

723
01:00:38,961 --> 01:00:42,082
I mean these are the people, who should be paying Thirty Pound Fine.

724
01:00:42,656 --> 01:00:46,617
They are bumping into everyone causing traffic hazards

725
01:00:48,059 --> 01:00:50,545
because they are so concentrating in that book of Dua(دُعَا).

726
01:00:53,345 --> 01:00:59,942
And they are causing harm to the Muslims, in Tawaf(طواف).

727
01:01:02,808 --> 01:01:05,304
A brother was just telling me that he was reading a book on Hajj(حَجْ)

728
01:01:05,714 --> 01:01:09,093
and the author was saying again and again, Do not harm the Muslims,

729
01:01:09,193 --> 01:01:11,914
Do not harm the Muslims, Do not harm the Muslims.

730
01:01:13,417 --> 01:01:16,260
Don’t cause them hardship because you want to finish your book.

731
01:01:18,095 --> 01:01:23,043
Now, this man may be he doesn’t understand that Dua(دُعَا) it's in Arabic

732
01:01:23,068 --> 01:01:25,043
and probably this person doesn’t speak Arabic,

733
01:01:26,473 --> 01:01:29,450
many Arabs do also reads those Dua(دُعَا) and may be they don’t understand what is in it.

734
01:01:32,325 --> 01:01:33,973
So, they don’t have khushu(خشوع)

735
01:01:35,135 --> 01:01:41,347
and everybody around them, is having a problem because of this, that’s not a Dua(دُعَا).

736
01:01:42,883 --> 01:01:45,585
Make any Dua(دُعَا) can’t you say O Allaah forgive me!

737
01:01:46,460 --> 01:01:48,129
Can’t you say O Allaah have a mercy on me,

738
01:01:48,317 --> 01:01:49,904
Can’t you say O Allaah grant me Jannah(جنة),

739
01:01:49,975 --> 01:01:52,264
Does it take a scholar to make such a Dua(دُعَا).

740
01:01:52,776 --> 01:01:54,017
Anybody can make it.

741
01:01:54,959 --> 01:01:59,736
If that book, the Dua(دُعَا) in it wasn’t written by Rasool Allahﷺ,

742
01:01:59,912 --> 01:02:02,048
why is it binding on you to read it?

743
01:02:04,010 --> 01:02:08,592
It is preferring symbols over substance,

744
01:02:09,532 --> 01:02:12,680
no I have to finish this book.

745
01:02:13,297 --> 01:02:17,427
Allahعَزّوجَلّ does not want to hear a Dua(دُعَا) from you that you don’t understand.

746
01:02:18,354 --> 01:02:21,049
How will Allaah respond to a Dua(دُعَا) that you making it

747
01:02:21,074 --> 01:02:22,514
if you don’t know what you are asking for?

748
01:02:23,924 --> 01:02:25,806
You know Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) it doesn’t make any sense at all.

749
01:02:27,933 --> 01:02:31,846
The essence of Dua(دُعَا) is that your heart should be connected to your tongue

750
01:02:32,378 --> 01:02:35,149
when you make the Dua(دُعَا) and you should have khushu(خشوع)

751
01:02:35,530 --> 01:02:41,289
and you should humble yourself and ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ and beg Allahعَزّوجَلّ to accept your Dua(دُعَا).

752
01:02:42,288 --> 01:02:43,493
اَلْاِلْحَافْ فِي الدُّعَا

753
01:02:43,525 --> 01:02:47,206
That’s one of the reasons why Dua(دُعَا) is accepted, when you persists in Dua(دُعَا).

754
01:02:47,999 --> 01:02:50,620
That persistence means that you repeat it again and again

755
01:02:50,859 --> 01:02:56,135
you do it with enthusiasm with commitment and with humbleness

756
01:02:58,350 --> 01:03:00,346
and you are begging Allahعَزّوجَلّ to give you that.

757
01:03:03,710 --> 01:03:05,709
So, you can make any Dhikar(زكر) you can make any Dua(دُعَا)

758
01:03:05,734 --> 01:03:09,748
it doesn’t have to be from that book.

759
01:03:27,458 --> 01:03:28,513
Al-Hajj(حَجْ);

760
01:03:29,963 --> 01:03:35,892
He was also concerned with the Muslims who were not making Hajj(حَجْ). He said,

761
01:03:35,940 --> 01:03:39,936
لَقَدْ هَمَمْتُ اَنْ اَبْعَثَ رِجَالًا اِلَى هَذِهِ الْاَمْسَارْ

762
01:03:40,390 --> 01:03:46,939
فَيَنْظُرُاِلَى كُلِّ مَنْ كَانَ عِنْدَه’ جِدَّ فَلَمْ يَحُجَّ فَيَضْرِبُوْا عَلَيْهِمُ الْجِزْيَهْ

763
01:03:47,253 --> 01:03:51,189
وَمَا هُمْ بِمُسْلِمِيْنَ! مَا هُمْ بِمُسْلِمِيْنْ! مَا هُمْ بِمُسْلِمِيْن

764
01:03:53,060 --> 01:04:00,993
I was thinking about, I was considering sending men to different Muslim States

765
01:04:01,981 --> 01:04:05,906
to see the Muslims who are able to make Hajj(حَجْ) and didn’t make Hajj(حَجْ)

766
01:04:06,426 --> 01:04:10,378
and to have them pay Jizya(جزية) because they are not Muslim,

767
01:04:10,504 --> 01:04:12,880
They are not Muslim! They are not Muslim.

768
01:04:16,209 --> 01:04:18,238
According to many of the scholars,

769
01:04:18,303 --> 01:04:20,221
اَلْحَجْ وَاجِبٌ عَلَى الْفَوْرَ

770
01:04:20,887 --> 01:04:24,792
Hajj(حَجْ) is mandatory immediately, this year if you are able to make it.

771
01:04:26,471 --> 01:04:32,866
If you have the financial ability you are strong and you can make time for it

772
01:04:34,477 --> 01:04:39,373
and you didn’t make Hajj(حَجْ) that’s a sin, according to many of the scholars.

773
01:04:40,024 --> 01:04:48,295
According to Ash-Shafi'e(الشافعى), it is mandatory but any time you can make it,

774
01:04:48,381 --> 01:04:54,752
however, Ash-Shafi'e(الشافعى) says if you die and you didn’t make it

775
01:04:55,396 --> 01:05:00,255
and there was a year in which you were able to make it, then you are dying in the state of sin.

776
01:05:00,536 --> 01:05:05,130
So, even though he says that you can make it later but he said;

777
01:05:05,155 --> 01:05:08,653
If death comes to you and you didn’t do it then you will be held accountable for that.

778
01:05:10,050 --> 01:05:14,145
And this is talking about anyone who is above the age of puberty.

779
01:05:16,799 --> 01:05:20,800
If you are able to make Hajj(حَجْ) you have the financial resources to Hajj(حَجْ)

780
01:05:21,124 --> 01:05:28,406
and you don’t do it, you have to pay Jizyah(جزية), according to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب).

781
01:05:30,160 --> 01:05:31,564
So, make sure that you do Hajj(حَجْ),

782
01:05:32,705 --> 01:05:37,431
plan for it this year, if you can if you have still time, well it's getting close

783
01:05:38,165 --> 01:05:39,476
but don’t delay Hajj(حَجْ).

784
01:05:39,600 --> 01:05:42,570
Do not delay Hajj(حَجْ) it's one of the Five Pillars of Islam

785
01:05:45,669 --> 01:05:52,546
and Hajj(حَجْ) is so great, it will forgive for you all of your past sins, all of them.

786
01:05:55,674 --> 01:06:00,788
Amr Bin Al-Aas رضي الله عنه, he came to give the Pledge of Allegiance to Rasool Allah ﷺ

787
01:06:00,812 --> 01:06:03,154
when he wanted to become a Muslim, he came to Rasool Ullah and said,

788
01:06:03,179 --> 01:06:04,683
O Rasool Ullah: I want to become a Muslim.

789
01:06:05,996 --> 01:06:09,887
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ extended his hand,

790
01:06:11,944 --> 01:06:13,710
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) pulled his hand away.

791
01:06:15,343 --> 01:06:16,972
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him what's wrong?

792
01:06:17,506 --> 01:06:19,464
Now, Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) was a diplomat,

793
01:06:21,744 --> 01:06:28,591
he was the man Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) would send around to negotiate with the leaders.

794
01:06:29,480 --> 01:06:33,311
So he wanted to negotiate his Islam with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

795
01:06:34,114 --> 01:06:39,853
You know he was evening thinking about negotiations when he wanted to become a Muslim رضى الله عنه.

796
01:06:40,433 --> 01:06:42,598
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him why did you hold your hand back?

797
01:06:42,622 --> 01:06:44,605
He said: Because I have some conditions to make.

798
01:06:45,798 --> 01:06:47,554
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: What conditions?

799
01:06:48,131 --> 01:06:53,300
He said, that you pardon me, for my sins.

800
01:06:53,962 --> 01:06:56,948
That my sins are pardoned.

801
01:06:59,646 --> 01:07:04,306
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) knew that he has been such an enemy of Islam,

802
01:07:04,952 --> 01:07:10,331
that he deserves to be executed because of what he has done.

803
01:07:11,310 --> 01:07:13,778
So, he wants to make sure that Rasool Ullah will give him clemency,

804
01:07:14,542 --> 01:07:17,269
and he is not going to be held accountable for what he did in the past.

805
01:07:18,238 --> 01:07:19,867
Rasool Allah ﷺ smiled and said;

806
01:07:19,891 --> 01:07:28,943
ياعمرو عَمَا تَعْلَمْ ؟اَنَّالْاِسْلَامَ يَجُبُّ مَا قَبْلَهَا، وَاَنَّ الْهِجْرَ ةَ تَجُبُّ مَا قَبْلَهَا، وَاَنَّ الْحَجَّ يَجُبُّ مَا قَبْلَهَا

807
01:07:29,908 --> 01:07:34,148
O Amr(عمرو) didn’t you know that Islam erases everything before it,

808
01:07:34,926 --> 01:07:40,539
and Hijrah(هجرة) erases everything before it, and Hajj(حَجْ) erases everything before it.

809
01:07:42,241 --> 01:07:46,530
Hajj(حَجْ) will erase everything that you did before and you will come back as if you are day born.

810
01:07:46,845 --> 01:07:48,762
رَجَعَكَ يَوْمِ وَلَدَتْه’ اُمُّ

811
01:07:50,145 --> 01:07:50,955
So, make Hajj(حَجْ).

812
01:07:53,991 --> 01:07:58,062
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) himself, he would lead the Hajj(حَجْ) every year,

813
01:07:59,437 --> 01:08:03,009
so they said, he made Hajj(حَجْ) when he was Khalifah(خليفه) Nine or Ten Times.

814
01:08:03,890 --> 01:08:06,080
He would lead the Hajj(حَجْ) himself.

815
01:08:06,859 --> 01:08:12,536
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه would give a lot of attention

816
01:08:12,959 --> 01:08:20,160
to the Financial Aspects of the Khilafah(خِلَافَه), the business, the commerce,

817
01:08:20,830 --> 01:08:22,946
Anas bin Malik رضى الله عنه  said:

818
01:08:22,970 --> 01:08:24,372
رَأَيْتُ عَلى عمر ابن الخطاب

819
01:08:24,396 --> 01:08:26,808
I saw Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) wearing an Izaar(إزار)

820
01:08:28,060 --> 01:08:38,543
and it had twelve patches in it and he didn’t have any Qamees(قميص) on him

821
01:08:39,346 --> 01:08:42,849
and he was wearing his turban and carrying his stick

822
01:08:43,418 --> 01:08:50,193
and he would go around the market of Madina, inspecting the market.

823
01:08:51,142 --> 01:08:52,807
He would go and inspect the market

824
01:08:53,454 --> 01:08:58,075
and he would tell the Businessmen in the market of Madina:

825
01:08:58,377 --> 01:09:04,104
لَايَبِعْ فِيْ سُوْقِنَااِلَّا مَنْ تَفَقَّهَا وَاِلَّا اَكَلَ الرِّبَا اشَاءًاَبَا

826
01:09:04,798 --> 01:09:10,130
You are not allowed to sell in our market place unless you have Fiqh(فقه)

827
01:09:11,853 --> 01:09:18,218
otherwise, you will deal with interest, Riba(رباء) whether you like it or not.

828
01:09:20,318 --> 01:09:26,205
So, he said: You have to learn the Fiqh(فقه) of business before you sell in our markets,

829
01:09:26,412 --> 01:09:27,900
like you have to have certificate

830
01:09:28,865 --> 01:09:35,327
that you have studied the Fiqh(فقه) of business before you come in and do trade.

831
01:09:36,604 --> 01:09:41,420
So, just like now you are not allowed to work unless you have a certificate

832
01:09:42,065 --> 01:09:43,777
unless you graduated in that field

833
01:09:44,099 --> 01:09:49,187
same thing Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) wanted to know that they were qualified to practice in the market

834
01:09:50,204 --> 01:09:57,463
 and that applies to you today, if you are physician you need to study the Fiqh(فقه) relating to your field

835
01:09:57,872 --> 01:10:04,143
you need to study the aspects of Daa(داء) and Dawa(دوا), the illness and the medicine in Islam.

836
01:10:04,657 --> 01:10:06,148
What is the Islamic Medicine?

837
01:10:06,487 --> 01:10:08,154
 What is considered to be an illness?

838
01:10:08,533 --> 01:10:10,152
How to cure in Islam?

839
01:10:10,192 --> 01:10:14,608
That will help in your field, you need to know rules regarding, for example

840
01:10:14,878 --> 01:10:17,475
abortion when it is allowed and when it is not allowed,

841
01:10:17,792 --> 01:10:23,944
contraception all of these issues that would relate to a specific field

842
01:10:24,453 --> 01:10:26,512
 you need to learn about them.

843
01:10:29,969 --> 01:10:34,061
If you are a farmer you need to learn the rules regarding farming.

844
01:10:34,965 --> 01:10:37,459
If you are a businessman depending upon the field of your business,

845
01:10:37,564 --> 01:10:40,040
you need to learn the Ahkam(أحكام) relating to that.

846
01:10:40,065 --> 01:10:44,548
And if you real estate agent you need to know, what is Halal(حلال) in that field and what is Haram(حرام)?

847
01:10:44,903 --> 01:10:46,649
What involves Riba(ربا) and what doesn’t?

848
01:10:47,731 --> 01:10:49,977
Not only in your field of profession

849
01:10:50,169 --> 01:10:53,113
but as a husband you need to know what your responsibilities are?

850
01:10:53,403 --> 01:10:56,183
As a wife you need to know what your responsibilities are?

851
01:10:56,541 --> 01:10:59,053
Notice here that I am saying, RESPONSIBILITIES not RIGHTS.

852
01:11:00,845 --> 01:11:04,756
In the West you are always told to fight for your Rights,

853
01:11:05,716 --> 01:11:10,936
so the man and woman come into marriage with the will to fight for their rights.

854
01:11:12,362 --> 01:11:16,236
The man is fighting for his rights, the woman is fighting for her rights

855
01:11:16,838 --> 01:11:19,462
and it's like, you are in a bull ring.

856
01:11:27,036 --> 01:11:32,152
A Muslim asks about their responsibilities not rights.

857
01:11:33,252 --> 01:11:35,716
You are asked about your responsibilities towards others.

858
01:11:36,369 --> 01:11:43,230
If the wife takes care of her responsibilities and the husband take care of his responsibilities

859
01:11:43,748 --> 01:11:44,853
there will be no problems.

860
01:11:45,740 --> 01:11:51,842
You get problems when you start fighting for your rights it's not a boxing arena

861
01:11:53,364 --> 01:11:58,945
marriage is a cooperation, it is a ibadaa(عبادة) you are serving Allah through that relationship.

862
01:12:00,809 --> 01:12:03,517
The parents needs to learn their responsibilities

863
01:12:04,621 --> 01:12:07,992
and the children need to learn their responsibilities all of this is Fiqh(فقه)

864
01:12:08,457 --> 01:12:09,838
that needs to be studied.

865
01:12:12,319 --> 01:12:14,534
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) wanted the people to work, He said;

866
01:12:14,647 --> 01:12:20,638
مَكْسَبَ فِيْهَا بَعْدَ الدَّنَاءْ خَيْرًا مِّنْ مَسْئَلَه’ خَيْرًامِّنْ مَّسْئَلَةْ النَّاْس

867
01:12:22,447 --> 01:12:29,894
Having a work that is of low reputation is better than begging people.

868
01:12:31,215 --> 01:12:36,090
Working in a particular field that has a bad reputation, low reputation.

869
01:12:36,133 --> 01:12:37,311
I am not talking about something Haram(حرام)

870
01:12:37,574 --> 01:12:41,655
but there are some things that are Halal(حلال) that are viewed as lowly,

871
01:12:43,034 --> 01:12:47,212
as humble, as humiliating but they are Halal(حلال).

872
01:12:47,536 --> 01:12:49,868
Umar(عُمَر) is saying that is better than begging people.

873
01:12:52,683 --> 01:13:00,429
Living on welfare is worse than working in something that is belittled by people.

874
01:13:05,380 --> 01:13:11,513
Now, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) would go to the poor and would say;

875
01:13:12,103 --> 01:13:15,421
إرفعوايامعشرالفقراء ارفعوا رءوسكم

876
01:13:17,393 --> 01:13:22,026
و تجرو افقد وضعك طريق ولاتكونواايالاالناس

877
01:13:22,663 --> 01:13:32,879
O you the poor! Raise up your heads and go and do business because the path is clear

878
01:13:33,349 --> 01:13:35,809
and don’t be dependent on people.

879
01:13:39,311 --> 01:13:42,308
You know, sometimes you cannot blame poor for not working

880
01:13:44,018 --> 01:13:46,492
because they are put in such a depressed state

881
01:13:47,839 --> 01:13:51,476
 and they have nowhere to start from that they lose hope

882
01:13:52,666 --> 01:13:57,970
and they become down, you know they just give up.

883
01:13:59,484 --> 01:14:04,773
Umar(عمر) is trying to encourage them, he said, riseup, look up raise your heads up

884
01:14:05,495 --> 01:14:08,296
and go and trade, start somewhere,

885
01:14:10,094 --> 01:14:12,887
and then he said, that is better than being dependent on others.

886
01:14:13,485 --> 01:14:17,351
So, the poor needs to be given encouragement because when you are poor

887
01:14:17,375 --> 01:14:20,153
and all the doors of opportunities are shutting on your face

888
01:14:20,526 --> 01:14:22,427
that is very difficult psychological state.

889
01:14:23,459 --> 01:14:24,311
You lose hope.

890
01:14:24,832 --> 01:14:26,360
So, Umar(عمر) is trying to encourage them.

891
01:14:27,452 --> 01:14:30,163
You know, sometimes we talk about working and working and working

892
01:14:30,187 --> 01:14:33,245
the brother comes and says I have been trying to do work but there is no work to do.

893
01:14:34,998 --> 01:14:37,037
So, such a brother needs to be encouraged.

894
01:14:37,061 --> 01:14:39,606
You know keep on trying keep on trying ask Allah

895
01:14:39,861 --> 01:14:42,588
it’s a test from Allahعَزّوجَلّ for you, keep on trying.

896
01:14:46,346 --> 01:14:52,074
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه saw some people who were not working, they were in the Masjid(مسجد),

897
01:14:52,114 --> 01:14:53,630
 you now they were just sitting in the Masjid(مسجد)

898
01:14:54,569 --> 01:14:57,463
and they were sitting in the Masjid(مسجد) during the business hours.

899
01:14:58,338 --> 01:15:00,893
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) goes in and said: What are you doing in the Masjid(مسجد),

900
01:15:00,918 --> 01:15:01,760
it's not a time for Salah(صلاة)?

901
01:15:03,901 --> 01:15:06,466
They said: We put our trust in Allah, Allah is going to give us Rizq(رزق).

902
01:15:07,587 --> 01:15:08,373
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said:

903
01:15:08,398 --> 01:15:11,685
لا يقعداحدكم انت طلب الرزق ويقول اللهم الرزقني

904
01:15:12,167 --> 01:15:15,301
وقد علم ان السمآء لا تمطرالذهب ولا فضة

905
01:15:15,766 --> 01:15:22,548
وانالله يرزق الناس بعضهم من بعض وتل قول الله تعالى عزوجل

906
01:15:22,585 --> 01:15:29,940
فإذا قضيت الصلاة فانتشروافي الارض وبتغوا من فضل الله واذكروا الله كثيرا لعلكم تفلحون۝

907
01:15:31,976 --> 01:15:39,609
He said: Don’t sit down without doing any work, and then say, "O Allah give me Rizq(رزق)!"

908
01:15:40,664 --> 01:15:44,471
because you know that the sky does not rain gold and silver

909
01:15:46,363 --> 01:15:48,987
and then he recited the Ayah(آية) in Qur’an

910
01:15:49,390 --> 01:15:53,411
"when Salah(صلاة) is over, Salaat ul Jumu'a(صلاة الجمعه) is over, go out and disperse in the land

911
01:15:53,804 --> 01:15:55,392
and seek the bounties of Allah.

912
01:15:55,616 --> 01:15:56,416
 "Go out and work."

913
01:15:56,640 --> 01:15:57,463
And then he said,

914
01:15:57,632 --> 01:16:00,557
Because Allah gives the people Rizq(رزق) from each other.

915
01:16:02,129 --> 01:16:05,459
Your Rizq(رزق) is coming from me and my Rizq(رزق) is coming from that person

916
01:16:05,659 --> 01:16:07,714
we work for each other, we serve each other.

917
01:16:08,244 --> 01:16:11,313
See this money that you have in your pocket

918
01:16:11,409 --> 01:16:13,767
it has passed through how many hands before it reaches you.

919
01:16:14,938 --> 01:16:17,613
so our Rizq(رزق) comes from each other.

920
01:16:17,653 --> 01:16:18,940
It's rotating among us.

921
01:16:19,035 --> 01:16:20,874
كاولئك دولة بين الاغني منكم

922
01:16:21,697 --> 01:16:22,751
The money is going around.

923
01:16:24,249 --> 01:16:28,077
IT SHUDDERS IN PAIN FREELY

924
01:16:28,537 --> 01:16:32,352
MY CHASITY, MY MODESTY!

925
01:16:32,756 --> 01:16:36,221
OH MUSLIM, YOU SAW

926
01:16:37,162 --> 01:16:41,228
MY INJURY AND THE INJURY OF MY PRIDE

